target:    admin/index.php
gate:      php tests/textdomain-single-source-test.php
kind:      guard-removal
expect:    is called with no text domain
rationale: Drop the text domain entirely. WordPress then looks the string up in core's 'default' domain, so it either falls back to English or - worse - picks up core's translation of an unrelated string that happens to share the msgid. Two calls in this file were in exactly that state and nothing had ever reported them; this gate found them on its first real run.
---
--- a/admin/index.php
+++ b/admin/index.php
@@ -169,7 +169,7 @@
             'inactive' => [
                 'is_report_group' => true,
                 'show_in_sidebar' => false,
-                'title'           => __('Inactive Reports', 'wp-slimstat'),
+                'title'           => __('Inactive Reports'),
                 'capability'      => '',
                 'callback'        => '', // No callback and capabilities are needed if show_in_sidebar is false
             ],
